# ALL.mask -- CEO-409 line masks for ProPuzzles, declared beside the data (FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason; a row with an empty
# reason is REFUSED). Read by corpus_suite_harness.py read_mask_sidecar()/masks_for(). Each regex matches a line that prints an unbound
# variable, in either stream: swipl's _22836 and SCRIP's _G0 both become the marker, so a line SCRIP omits or adds still reds.
# hq_prolog 2026-10-25: the three entries whose only divergence from the ref is a printed variable name (alphametic 5 of 49 lines,
# extract_from_indices 1 of 8, isbn 1 of 40, guardrail 4's half far off).
hakank_swi_alphametic	(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])_G?[0-9]+(?![A-Za-z0-9_])	a fresh variable's written name is implementation-defined (ISO 7.10.5); swipl 9.0.4 prints _N, a number taken from where the variable lives, and the number moves between runs of the same file (measured 2026-10-25, hq_prolog: alphametic's first variable line reads _22836 in the ref cut at the container build and _20930 on a rerun); SCRIP prints _G<n>. Every other line of the entry is graded (CEO-409)
hakank_swi_extract_from_indices	(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])_G?[0-9]+(?![A-Za-z0-9_])	a fresh variable's written name is implementation-defined (ISO 7.10.5); swipl 9.0.4 prints _N, a number taken from where the variable lives, and the number moves between runs of the same file (measured 2026-10-25, hq_prolog: alphametic's first variable line reads _22836 in the ref cut at the container build and _20930 on a rerun); SCRIP prints _G<n>. Every other line of the entry is graded (CEO-409)
hakank_swi_isbn	(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])_G?[0-9]+(?![A-Za-z0-9_])	a fresh variable's written name is implementation-defined (ISO 7.10.5); swipl 9.0.4 prints _N, a number taken from where the variable lives, and the number moves between runs of the same file (measured 2026-10-25, hq_prolog: alphametic's first variable line reads _22836 in the ref cut at the container build and _20930 on a rerun); SCRIP prints _G<n>. Every other line of the entry is graded (CEO-409)
hakank_swi_send_more_money	(?<![A-Za-z0-9_])_G?[0-9]+(?![A-Za-z0-9_])	a fresh variable's written name is implementation-defined (ISO 7.10.5); swipl 9.0.4 prints _N, a number taken from where the variable lives, and the number moves between runs of the same file (the same measurement as alphametic's, 2026-10-25); SCRIP prints _G<n>. Measured 2026-10-28, hq_prolog: send_more_money's FIRST line reads digits_before=[9,_16312,_16404,_16496,1,0,_16772,_16864] in the ref and digits_before=[9,_G0,_G1,_G2,1,0,_G3,_G4] in SCRIP, in both modes; the other two lines are identical and are graded (CEO-409)
